The text 'remove plate' in orange is placed near the arrow, explaining the =
operation.  Both sides use bold, black, rectangular shapes to represent the=
 plates, clearly showing the stack's Last-In, First-Out (LIFO) nature." loa=
ding=3D"lazy" width=3D"402" height=3D"148" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"=
1" style=3D"color:transparent" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/images/courses=
