pl=3Ddpl_CEjisbLnWxFQGUTRjiHGoKY1oV5c"></div></figure>
<p>This analogy encapsulates the essence of the stack data structure. Addin=
g a plate to and taking a plate from the top of the stack, physically demon=
strates the two main stack operations:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Push</strong> (adds an element to the top of the stack).</li>
<li><strong>Pop</strong> (removes and returns the element at the top of the=
 stack).</li>
</ul>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
img alt=3D"Image represents a visual depiction of stack data structure oper=
