Each stack is represented as a container, with the numbers inside represent=
ing the elements, and the newest element added at the top.  A light-blue ar=
row labeled 'push(x)' indicates the addition of element 'x' to the stack. T=
he bottom row illustrates the `pop` operation, where elements are removed f=
rom the top of the stack from left to right. A purple arrow labeled 'pop' s=
hows the removal of the top element.  The numbers within the stack containe=
rs change accordingly to reflect the addition or removal of elements, demon=
strating the Last-In, First-Out (LIFO) nature of a stack.  The label 'stack=
' is present below each container to clearly identify the data structure." =
